{%- comment -%}
  Outputs an absolute https URL for the brand logo, for use in schema.org
  Organization / ImageObject logo properties.

  Google requires a structured data logo to be at least 112x112px, and Shopify's
  CDN cannot resize or rasterize SVG. settings.logo is an SVG with no width or
  height attributes, so there is nothing for Google to measure. When the logo is
  an SVG, fall back to settings.favicon, which is a square raster image.

  Outputs an empty string when neither setting has an image, so callers should
  only emit the logo property when the captured value is present.

  Usage:
  {%- capture logo_url -%}{%- render 'seo-logo-url' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign logo_url = logo_url | strip -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign logo_source = settings.logo
  assign logo_probe = settings.logo | image_url: width: 100
  if settings.logo == blank or logo_probe contains '.svg'
    assign logo_source = settings.favicon
  endif

  if logo_source != blank
    echo logo_source | image_url: width: 512 | prepend: 'https:'
  endif
-%}
